.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt RINGMASTER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ringmaster
.Nd llama-server control-plane daemon and background-job platform
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm daemon
.Op Fl -socket Ar path
.Nm
.Cm start
.Op Fl -target Ar session-key
.Op Fl -label Ar label
.Op Fl -source Ar source
.Nm
.Cm progress Ar job-id
.Op Fl -message Ar message
.Nm
.Cm done Ar job-id
.Fl -state Ar succeeded | failed | cancelled | interrupted
.Op Fl -message Ar message
.Op Fl -result-ref Ar ref
.Op Fl -resource Ar uri
.Nm
.Cm read
.Op Fl -job Ar job-id
.Op Fl -since Ar ts
.Op Fl -type Ar type
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm spool-path Ar job-id
.Op Fl -target Ar session-key
.Nm
.Cm status Ar job-id
.Op Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id
.Op Fl -tail Ar n
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm wait Ar job-id
.Op Fl -target Ar session-key
.Op Fl -timeout Ar dur
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm whoami
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm ls
.Op Fl -target Ar key
.Op Fl -all
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm tail Ar job-id
.Op Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl n Ar lines
.Nm
.Cm cancel Ar job-id
.Op Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id
.Op Fl -message Ar text
.Nm
.Cm monitor
.Op Fl -once
.Op Fl -session Ar session-key
.Nm
.Cm mcp
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is clown's background-job platform (RFC-0015) and the control-plane daemon for
.Xr llama-server 1
instances (FDR-0010).
The two roles are one hat: a supervised
.Xr llama-server 1
is a specialized kind of job the platform runs.
.Pp
As the
.Em daemon ,
.Nm
is a long-lived per-user process that spawns and supervises
.Xr llama-server 1
children on behalf of clients such as
.Xr circus 1
and
.Xr clown 1 ,
talking to them over a Unix domain socket using newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0.
See
.Xr ringmaster 7
for the architecture.
.Pp
As the
.Em job platform ,
.Nm
carries the producer/agent surface \(em
.Cm start , progress , done , read , spool-path , wait ,
and
.Cm whoami
\(em promoted from the former
.Li clown job
subcommands (RFC-0015), plus the operator surface \(em
.Cm ls , status , tail ,
and
.Cm cancel
\(em for inspecting and cancelling jobs out of band, and the internal
.Cm monitor
and
.Cm mcp
entrypoints clown synthesizes.
These need no running daemon; they read and append to the on-disk job journal
directly.
The messaging half of the platform (chat and the standalone waking message) is
the separate
.Xr troupe 1
binary.
.Pp
The wakeup channel has two layers so that
.Em correctness
.Pq never lose a wakeup
comes from disk durability while
.Em liveness
.Pq sub-second latency
comes from a best-effort socket free to drop: an append-only on-disk journal
under
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/jobs/
is the at-least-once source of truth, and a lossy Unix-domain datagram nudge
under
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/jobs/
pokes the monitor to re-read it.
The
.Em waking
events \(em those surfaced as a notification \(em are the four terminal types
.Pq Li succeeded , failed , cancelled , interrupted
plus the non-terminal
.Li message
type; the
.Li started
and
.Li progress
events are journal-only.
.Pp
A single job is addressed two ways for the operator subcommands.
.Fl -target
takes a session key the operator holds and hashes it to a channel (see
.Sx SESSION KEY ) .
.Fl -channel
takes a raw channel id directly \(em the value
.Cm ls Fl -all
prints \(em so an operator can act on a job in a session whose key it does not
hold; the channel id is a one-way hash of the session key.
The two are mutually exclusive, and a
.Fl -channel
that is not lowercase hex is rejected as a usage error.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm daemon Op Fl -socket Ar path
Run the control-plane daemon.
Listens on the path resolved from
.Fl -socket
when present, the
.Ev RINGMASTER_SOCKET
environment variable when set, or
.Pa $HOME/.local/state/circus/control.sock
otherwise.
Accepts connections until SIGTERM/SIGINT, at which point in-flight RPCs drain
and the listener closes.
.It Cm start Oo Fl -target Ar session-key Oc Oo Fl -label Ar label Oc Oo Fl -source Ar source Oc
Allocate a job id, create the job's journal file, append the
.Li started
record, and print the job id.
With
.Fl -label
the id is
.Ar sanitized-label Ns Li - Ns Ar 8-hex .
With
.Fl -target
the journal is created for another session's channel (the external-wakeup
case).
.Fl -source
labels the emitting plugin and is carried verbatim in every record.
.It Cm progress Ar job-id Oo Fl -message Ar message Oc
Append a journal-only
.Li progress
record.
Recorded and observable but never wakes the agent.
.It Cm done Ar job-id Fl -state Ar state Oo Fl -message Ar message Oc Oo Fl -result-ref Ar ref Oc Oo Fl -resource Ar uri Oc
Append the job's single terminal record and send the nudge.
.Ar state
must be one of
.Li succeeded , failed , cancelled ,
or
.Li interrupted .
Exits non-zero without appending if the job already has a terminal record.
.Fl -result-ref
is an opaque pointer surfaced to the agent as text.
.Fl -resource
attaches a resource reference (a
.Li madder://blobs/ Ns Ar digest
URI or any fetchable URI), repeatable (clown#112); clown carries the reference
only and the consumer fetches each URI.
.It Cm read Oo Fl -job Ar job-id Oc Oo Fl -since Ar ts Oc Oo Fl -type Ar type Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
The pull / observability surface for this session's channel.
With
.Fl -job
it prints that job's full record stream; without it, it scans the channel for
waking events, optionally filtered by
.Fl -since
.Pq an exclusive RFC 3339 lower bound
and repeatable
.Fl -type .
Each record prints as a notification line (see
.Sx NOTIFICATION LINE ) ,
or one JSON object per line with
.Fl -json .
.It Cm spool-path Ar job-id Oo Fl -target Ar session-key Oc
Print the absolute path of the job's output spool \(em a producer-written,
append-only side file at
.Pa <job-id>.out
.Pq RFC-0010 .
The channel directory is created if absent, but the spool file itself is the
producer's append.
When the facility is disabled it prints nothing and exits
.Li 0 .
A malformed
.Ar job-id
is a usage error
.Pq exit Li 2 .
.It Cm status Ar job-id Oo Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id Oc Oo Fl -tail Ar n Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Report one job's status, derived from its journal and spool alone: state,
source, elapsed, last activity, spool bytes, newest progress message, and a
bounded tail
.Pq the last Ar n No lines, default 20 .
A read-only pull, available regardless of
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP .
The single
.Cm status
verb serves both the producer/agent and operator surfaces (RFC-0015 section 2),
so it accepts
.Fl -channel
as well as
.Fl -target .
With
.Fl -json
the status is one JSON object; otherwise a one-line header followed by the tail
under a
.Ql ---
separator.
A missing journal exits
.Li 1 ;
a malformed job id or channel id exits
.Li 2 .
.It Cm wait Ar job-id Oo Fl -target Ar session-key Oc Oo Fl -timeout Ar dur Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Block until the job reaches a terminal state, then print its status in exactly
the form
.Cm status
uses \(em the synchronous
.Em join
(clown#154).
It polls the journal rather than riding the nudge socket (a singleton owned by
the live monitor).
.Fl -timeout
bounds the wait
.Pq a Xr time 0 Ns -style duration; 0 blocks until terminal or Dv SIGINT Ns / Ns Dv SIGTERM .
An unknown job or a timeout exits
.Li 1 ;
a malformed id exits
.Li 2 ;
a signal is a clean exit
.Li 0 .
.It Cm whoami Op Fl -json
Print this clown instance's resolved identity: the per-instance session key, its
derived channel id, the precedence
.Em source
that supplied the key (see
.Sx SESSION KEY ) ,
and, when grouped, the group decoration
.Pq Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
and its derived group channel.
A pure read, available regardless of
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP .
.It Cm ls Oo Fl -target Ar key Oc Oo Fl -all Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
List background jobs as a table of job id, source, state, elapsed time, and
last activity.
By default lists the current session's channel;
.Fl -target
selects another session key, and
.Fl -all
spans every channel on the host, prefixing each row with its full channel id
\(em the exact value the action subcommands accept via
.Fl -channel .
.Fl -json
emits a JSON array.
.It Cm tail Ar job-id Oo Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id Oc Oo Fl f Oc Oo Fl n Ar lines Oc
Print the last
.Ar lines
.Pq default 20
lines of a job's output spool.
With
.Fl f ,
follow the spool until the job reaches a terminal state or the operator
interrupts.
A job absent from the resolved channel exits
.Li 1 ;
when an id from
.Cm ls Fl -all
names a job in another session, pass that row's
.Fl -channel .
.It Cm cancel Ar job-id Oo Fl -target Ar key | Fl -channel Ar id Oc Oo Fl -message Ar text Oc
Cooperatively cancel a job by writing its terminal
.Sq cancelled
record.
This wakes the originating session's monitor and signals the owning producer to
stop; see
.Sx CAVEATS .
A missing job, or one already terminal, exits
.Li 1 .
.It Cm monitor Op Fl -once Op Fl -session Ar session-key
Run the per-session channel wake monitor (RFC-0015 section 6, formerly
.Li clown job-watch ) .
It resolves the session key, replays any unacked waking events from the journal,
binds the nudge socket, then blocks, emitting one notification line per waking
event until
.Dv SIGINT Ns / Ns Dv SIGTERM
(a clean exit
.Li 0 ) .
It is a per-channel singleton (clown#132) and deliberately ignores stdin
(monitor hosts spawn it with an immediately-EOF stdin).
With
.Fl -once
it replays unacked events and exits without binding \(em the deterministic
conformance mode.
.Fl -session
overrides the resolved key with an explicit one;
.Nm clown
bakes it into the spawned monitor command (clown#136) so the key stays out of
the agent provider's environment.
Normally spawned by
.Nm clown
as a registered monitor, not run by hand.
.It Cm mcp
Serve the ringmaster tool surface of the job-platform MCP server (RFC-0011): a
stdio JSON-RPC server exposing the job-control tools
.Li job_start , job_progress , job_done , job_read , job_status , job_spool_path ,
and
.Li job_wait ,
surfaced to the agent as
.Li plugin:clown-builtin-jobs:ringmaster
and carrying the dynamic system-prompt fragment.
.Nm clown
synthesizes it as a
.Xr clown-json 5
stdioServers entry which
.Xr clown-stdio-bridge 1
wraps to streamable-HTTP; the messaging half is
.Xr troupe 1
.Cm mcp .
Not run by hand.
.El
.Sh SESSION KEY
A
.Em session key
names the agent session a wakeup is delivered to.
The active per-instance key is resolved in this order (RFC-0013 section 2.3):
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
if set and non-empty; otherwise
.Ev CLAUDE_SESSION_ID
if set and non-empty; otherwise a clown-generated UUIDv4.
.Pp
.Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
is
.Em not
in this precedence: it is the group
.Em decoration
(the
.Ar repo Ns Li / Ns Ar branch
label) naming the group of clown instances that share a worktree.
A message addressed to it fans out on the group channel
.Pq Li ChannelID Ns Pq Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID ,
which every clown under that group also watches.
The on-disk channel directory and nudge socket are named by a filesystem-safe
.Em channel id
derived from the session key \(em the first 16 bytes of its SHA-256 digest as 32
hex digits.
.Sh NOTIFICATION LINE
Each waking event the monitor emits \(em and each record
.Cm read
prints without
.Fl -json
\(em is a single line with no embedded newline:
.Pp
.Dl [clown-job] <source> <job-id> <type>: <message>
.Pp
When the record carries a
.Li from
(the sender key on a
.Li message
event), the segment
.Dq Li " from " <from>
is inserted before the colon.
The trailing
.Dq Li ": " <message>
is omitted when the record has no message.
When
.Li result_ref
is present,
.Dq Li " \(bu " <result_ref>
is appended; when the record carries
.Li resources
(clown#112),
.Dq Li " \(bu " <n> " resource(s)"
is appended as a count hint, the URIs recovered on the pull side via
.Cm read .
Any newline is flattened to a space so the one-line-per-event contract holds.
The channel guarantees each waking event is surfaced at least once, so consumers
MUST treat wakeups as idempotent, deduplicating on
.Pq Li job , Li type .
.Sh RPC SURFACE
The
.Cm daemon
implements seven JSON-RPC 2.0 methods:
.Cm StartInstance , StopInstance , StopAll , ListInstances , GetInstance ,
.Cm ListAvailableModels ,
and
.Cm DownloadModel .
.Cm StartInstance
spawns an
.Xr llama-server 1
child (resolving a bare model name to
.Pa ~/.local/share/circus/models/<model>.gguf )
and blocks until
.Pa /health
returns 200.
See
.Xr ringmaster 7
for the full method schemas.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGINT
.It Dv SIGTERM
The daemon drains in-flight RPCs and exits cleanly; children are NOT killed and
are re-adopted by the next
.Nm
process.
The
.Cm monitor
exits cleanly.
.It Dv SIGINT
Same as
.Dv SIGTERM .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RINGMASTER_SOCKET
Override the control socket path.
Both
.Nm
and its clients
.Pq Xr circus 1 , Xr clown 1
read it.
.It Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP
When set to
.Li 1 ,
the whole wakeup facility is disabled.
.Cm monitor
exits
.Li 0
immediately without binding a socket, and the emit subcommands
.Pq Cm start , progress , done
behave as no-ops that still exit
.Li 0 .
.Cm spool-path
prints nothing and exits
.Li 0 .
.Cm read , status , wait ,
and
.Cm whoami
still work, since they are pulls rather than emits.
.It Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
The highest-priority session-key source (see
.Sx SESSION KEY ) .
.It Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
The group decoration naming the group channel every clown under the group
watches.
.It Ev CLAUDE_SESSION_ID
Consulted when
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
is unset.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the durable journal
.Pq Pa clown/jobs/<channel-id>/ .
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the nudge socket.
.It Ev XDG_LOG_HOME
Resolves the daemon's log directory on macOS
.Pq Pa ~/.local/log/ringmaster.log
when unset.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.local/state/circus/control.sock
Default daemon control socket path.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/circus/models
Directory scanned for downloadable GGUF files.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/jobs/<channel-id>/<job-id>.jsonl
Per-job durable journal, one JSON record per line.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/jobs/<channel-id>/<job-id>.out
Per-job output spool: producer-written, append-only, best-effort live output.
.It Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/jobs/<channel-id>.sock
Per-channel nudge datagram socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li 0
The subcommand succeeded, or the facility was disabled via
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP ;
.Cm monitor
also exits
.Li 0
on a clean interrupt.
.It Li 1
A runtime failure (e.g. a journal write error,
.Cm done
on a job that already has a terminal record, or
.Cm status
for a job with no journal).
.It Li 2
A usage error: missing or unknown subcommand, a missing or malformed
.Ar job-id ,
a non-hex
.Fl -channel ,
or an invalid flag.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Background a long task and wake the originating session on completion:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
job=$(ringmaster start --source spinclass --label merge)
# ... run the long pre-merge hook ...
ringmaster done "$job" --state succeeded \e
  --message "merge landed on master" \e
  --result-ref "spinclass session-job-status"
.Ed
.Pp
The idle agent receives one notification:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[clown-job] spinclass merge-9f3c1a2b succeeded: merge landed on master \(bu spinclass session-job-status
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect and follow another session's job by raw channel:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ringmaster ls --all
ringmaster tail -f build-3f2ab1c9 --channel <hex>
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr circus 1 ,
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr llama-server 1 ,
.Xr troupe 1 ,
.Xr clown-json 5 ,
.Xr ringmaster 7 ,
.Xr ringmaster-testing 7
.Pp
The normative contracts are specified in
.Pa docs/rfcs/0009-job-wakeup-channel.md
(wakeup channel),
.Pa docs/rfcs/0010-job-output-spool-and-status.md
(spool and status),
.Pa docs/rfcs/0011-job-platform-mcp-tools.md
(MCP tools), and
.Pa docs/rfcs/0015-ringmaster-troupe-platform-binaries.md
(the ringmaster/troupe binary surface), within the clown source repository.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
single-Wait contract: only one goroutine inside the daemon ever calls
.Xr exec.Cmd.Wait 3
for each child; both the
.Cm StopInstance
path and the unexpected-exit reaper read the same
.Sq exited
channel.
.Pp
.Cm cancel
is cooperative, not forceful.
Background jobs are not spawned by
.Nm
and the journal deliberately records no worker PID, so
.Cm cancel
writes the terminal
.Sq cancelled
record rather than signalling a process.
The owning producer observes the cancellation and tears down its own process
tree.
A producer that has hard-crashed without writing a terminal record cannot be
reaped by
.Cm cancel ;
its journal is garbage-collected after the retention window.
